@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Stock implementation plan
+
+1. Introduce a 409 Conflict exception and REST mapping for stock/cart/order-state conflicts.
+2. Centralize the default product stock lookup and cart stock validation in the cart/order service layer, using the catalog product identity/SKU and merchant store. Validate the complete proposed cart before mutating or saving it; allow removals and decreases, reject additions/increases above stock, and preserve the existing cart on failure.
+3. Apply that validation to new carts, duplicate adds, single updates, and multi updates. Make multi updates all-or-nothing and retain untouched cart lines.
+4. Make checkout transactional and two-phase: resolve every ordered line to its catalog product/default availability, validate all quantities first, then decrement exactly those availabilities before creating the order. Roll back stock and order persistence on any failure, and support both anonymous and authenticated checkout through the shared service.
+5. Implement cancellation inventory restoration in the order-status transition service. Restore each order line once, reject any transition from CANCELED to another status with 409, and make repeated CANCELED idempotent. Ensure all status paths use the same transition logic.
+6. Make the v2 product mapper report `available` and `canBePurchased` only when merchant availability is enabled and stock is positive, while retaining merchant-disabled products as unavailable after restock.
+7. Add focused regression tests where practical, run formatting/compilation and the relevant unit/integration test suites, then inspect the diff and report verification honestly.
