+# Stock research
+
+## Requested behavior and stock source
+
+The stock exposed by `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` is the default, non-variant `ProductAvailability.productQuantity` selected by the v2 product-definition mapper. `ProductAvailability` is stored in `PRODUCT_AVAILABILITY`; the merchant-controlled availability flag is `ProductAvailability.productStatus` (and the product itself also has an availability flag).
+
+## Checkout
+
+- Both checkout routes are in `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`:
+  - `/api/v1/cart/{code}/checkout`
+  - `/api/v1/auth/cart/{code}/checkout`
+- They delegate to `OrderFacadeImpl.processOrder`, which builds the order from the cart and calls `OrderService.processOrder`.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java` currently calls payment processing and `this.create(order)` before inventory work. It then loops order products, calls `productService.getById(orderProduct.getId())`, and decrements every availability row. `OrderProduct.id` is the order-line id, not the catalog product id, so this can select the wrong product; variants/regions are also not selected consistently. Insufficient stock is logged only, so orders can be created and stock can become negative. There is no transactionally atomic preflight across the cart.
+- The inventory source and catalog lookup services are in `sm-core/.../ProductAvailabilityService*`, `ProductService`, and `ProductAvailabilityRepository`; product SKU lookup is available and must be scoped to the merchant. `ProductAvailabilityRepository.getBySku` also has an `OR`/`AND` precedence issue in its store-scoped query, so stock logic should use the product loaded for the store and its selected default availability rather than trusting that query for authorization.
+
+## Cart changes
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` handles add/create, single update, and multi update.
+- `createCartItem` checks availability rows for null/zero, but does not reject a requested quantity greater than stock and does not consistently combine the merchant flag with quantity.
+- `addItemsToShoppingCart` can increment an existing line before saving without checking the resulting quantity. The v1 `readableShoppingCart` path has a SKU comparison bug (`cartItem.getProduct().getSku().equals(item.getProduct())`) and likewise saves after incrementing without a resulting-stock check.
+- `updateCartItem` sets the requested quantity directly. `updateCartItems` builds a `HashSet` of updates and mutates entries as it validates, so a later invalid update can leave earlier in-memory changes; it also replaces the cart line-item set with only submitted entries, which is inconsistent with the documented partial multi-update behavior.
+- `modifyCart` removes/updates/adds and saves directly. `modifyCartMulti` calls `createCartItems` first, but then mutates and saves each existing line as it iterates. No all-or-nothing stock preflight exists.
+- `sm-shop-model/.../CartModificationException.java` is a plain runtime exception; `RestErrorHandler` maps `ServiceRuntimeException` to 400 and does not provide a 409 handler. A dedicated conflict exception/handler or equivalent is needed so stock conflicts are HTTP 409.
+
+## Order cancellation/status
+
+- `PUT /api/v1/private/orders/{id}/status` is in `OrderApi.java` and delegates to `OrderFacadeImpl.updateOrderStatus`.
+- `OrderFacadeImpl.updateOrderStatus` returns for the same status and otherwise only changes status/history. It does not restore inventory, does not reject transitions out of CANCELED, and does not protect restoration from duplicate cancellation through another status-history route.
+- `OrderServiceImpl` owns catalog inventory updates during order creation and is the appropriate shared service boundary for atomic decrement/restoration. The order model has `OrderProduct.productSku`/product identity and ordered quantity populated by `PersistableOrderProductPopulator`/`OrderProductPopulator`; this must be used instead of the order-line id.
+
+## Product availability response
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/catalog/product/ReadableProductDefinitionMapper.java` sets `canBePurchased` from `availability.getProductStatus()` and maps inventory quantity, but does not set it false when quantity is zero.
+- The v2 product response is assembled by `ProductFacadeV2Impl` and mapped through this mapper. The response's `available`/visible field comes from the product/definition availability flag, so the mapper must combine merchant availability with positive stock while preserving a merchant-disabled product as unavailable after restock.
+
+## Tests/build impact
+
+Relevant existing integration tests are under `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/cart` and `.../product`; order tests are under `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/order`. New regression coverage should exercise both checkout routes, cart atomicity, cancellation idempotence/status transitions, and v2 flags. The root Maven reactor has `sm-core-model`, `sm-core-modules`, `sm-core`, `sm-shop-model`, and `sm-shop`.
